+            "observation": "Resolves a model name against model_info_manager.local_model_metadata first, then the cached litellm price/context JSON database. When nothing matches it returns dict() (line 247) rather than a default capability/cost record, so an unknown model surfaces as an explicitly empty mapping. The only name-shortening path (lines 242-245) returns the shorter entry solely when its litellm_provider equals the requested prefix, so a bare name like aurora-1-mini cannot silently inherit meta/aurora-1-mini metadata."
+        },
+        {
+            "path": "aider/models.py",
+            "symbol": "ModelInfoManager.get_model_info",
+            "start_line": 249,
+            "end_line": 274,
+            "observation": "Combines the cached lookup with litellm.get_model_info. If litellm raises for an unmapped model (the exception mentioning model_prices_and_context_window.json) it is caught and swallowed, and the function falls through to 'return cached_info' (line 274) - which is {} for an unknown model. No cost, context-window or supports_* key is ever synthesized here, so 'unknown' cannot masquerade as 'known with permissive capabilities'."
+        },
+        {
+            "path": "aider/models.py",
+            "symbol": "Model.__init__",
+            "start_line": 330,
+            "end_line": 369,
+            "observation": "Stores the metadata lookup in self.info (line 348) and derives max_chat_history_tokens from 'self.info.get(\"max_input_tokens\") or 0' (line 354), clamped to the documented min 1024 / max 8192 band (line 357). For an unknown model info is empty, so the chat-history budget is the 1024-token sane default instead of an invented context window."
+        },
+        {
+            "path": "aider/models.py",
+            "symbol": "Model.configure_model_settings",
+            "start_line": 385,
+            "end_line": 435,
+            "observation": "Initializes accepts_settings to [] when it is None (lines 400-401) and only appends optional settings such as thinking_tokens/reasoning_effort for explicitly matched settings or openrouter models (lines 415-435). Local metadata registration therefore cannot silently switch on an unsupported capability, which is exactly what the contract asserts for meta/aurora-1-pro (accepts_settings == [] despite declared metadata)."
+        },
+        {
+            "path": "aider/models.py",
+            "symbol": "Model.get_repo_map_tokens",
+            "start_line": 782,
+            "end_line": 789,
+            "observation": "Returns the documented 1024-token default when info carries no max_input_tokens (lines 783-784, 785 guard). This is the second observable 'sane default' the contract pins: an unknown model gets 1024 repo-map tokens rather than a value inferred from a fabricated context window."
