+        {
+            "claim": "An unknown model is represented explicitly as an empty metadata mapping: ModelInfoManager.get_model_from_cached_json_db returns dict() and ModelInfoManager.get_model_info returns that empty dict when litellm has no mapping, so no cost/context/capability values are fabricated. Executed: 'meta/ghost-404' -> {} through both the manager and Model(...).info.",
+            "evidence_paths": [
+                "aider/models.py"
+            ]
+        },
+        {
+            "claim": "Registering the local metadata fixture is verbatim and minimal: register_litellm_models stores exactly the two declared entries (meta/aurora-1-mini with only max_input_tokens/litellm_provider/mode, meta/aurora-1-pro with an explicit supports_function_calling: false) into model_info_manager.local_model_metadata without adding, defaulting or deleting keys; lookup returns those entries unchanged, so missing keys stay absent rather than becoming permissive defaults.",
+            "evidence_paths": [
+                "aider/models.py"
+            ]
+        },
+        {
+            "claim": "Unknown model handling is announced, not silent: sanity_check_model returns True for 'meta/ghost-404' and emits the two explicit warnings ('Unknown which environment variables are required.' and 'Unknown context window size and costs, using sane defaults.'), while an unknown model also receives only documented sane defaults (max_chat_history_tokens == 1024, get_repo_map_tokens() == 1024) and claims no optional settings (accepts_settings == [], extra_params is None).",
+            "evidence_paths": [
+                "aider/models.py"
+            ]
+        },
+        {
+            "claim": "Metadata cannot silently enable unsupported capabilities: Model.configure_model_settings initializes accepts_settings to [] and only appends thinking_tokens/reasoning_effort via explicit model settings or openrouter name rules, so neither the partial fixture entry nor the entry declaring supports_function_calling: false yields any advertised optional setting; the explicit False is preserved as a bool False rather than being upgraded to True.",
+            "evidence_paths": [
+                "aider/models.py"
+            ]
+        },
+        {
+            "claim": "Lookup does not silently transfer another model's metadata: the prefix-stripping branch of get_model_from_cached_json_db requires the candidate entry's litellm_provider to equal the requested provider prefix, so querying the bare name 'aurora-1-mini' returns {} instead of inheriting 'meta/aurora-1-mini'.",
+            "evidence_paths": [
+                "aider/models.py"
+            ]
+        }
+    ],
+    "conclusion": "The contract holds for the new local model metadata fixture (.prale-eval/contract/local-model-metadata.json). Driving the real aider.models code shows explicit unknown-model handling at every layer: an undeclared model resolves to an explicit empty metadata dict ({}), is reported through sanity_check_model's explicit 'Unknown ...' warnings with a truthy problem flag, and receives only documented sane defaults (1024 chat-history/repo-map tokens) while claiming no optional settings (accepts_settings == []). Fixture-declared metadata is stored verbatim, so partial entries keep their missing capability/cost keys absent and an explicit supports_function_calling: false stays False - nothing silently claims an unsupported capability. The executable contract .prale-eval/contract/check_unknown_model_contract.py passes 7/7 assertions and emits the normalized result .prale-eval/contract/contract-report.json; no repository source, task metadata, lockfile or git configuration was modified.",
+    "validation": {
