+        "notes": "Executed from the repository root: 7/7 contract assertions passed (C1 registration verbatim, C2 unknown model -> {}, C3 no basename inheritance, C4 explicit sanity-check warnings + True, C5 sane 1024 defaults with accepts_settings == [], C6 partial fixture metadata exact with no invented keys, C7 explicit False capability preserved), exit code 0; the normalized report was written to .prale-eval/contract/contract-report.json with top-level status 'pass'. LIMITATION: the optional third-party dependencies of this checkout are not installed and dependency installation is out of scope, so the harness installs narrow in-process shims before importing aider.models - json5 missing -> JSON-plus-line-comment shim, oslex missing -> shlex-based join/split shim, litellm missing -> stub whose get_model_info raises the model_prices_and_context_window.json error for unmapped models and whose validate_environment returns {'keys_in_environment': False, 'missing_keys': []}. The aider.models code paths under test are the real repository code; only the third-party boundary is simulated, and the limitations are recorded verbatim in contract-report.json under environment.limitations. The run is hermetic: HOME is redirected to .prale-eval/contract/_home (all aider cache writes stay in the workspace) and outbound HTTP is disabled, so no network access or writes outside the workspace occur."
